SavanXP: no file system below the library.

The library serves SUN and POSIX programs alike and asks the program only for
what both runtimes give (ports/openssl/README.md). Built with no-stdio and
OPENSSL_NO_POSIX_IO, three places still reached the file system; here they
say "unsupported" instead:

- crypto/o_dir.c: directory listing is not implemented (LPdir_nyi.c, as on
  UEFI);
- crypto/rand/randfile.c: RAND_load_file and RAND_write_file have no seed
  file to read or write;
- providers/.../file_store.c: the "file:" store opens nothing.

Certificates reach the library in memory (PEM through a memory BIO).

diff -ru a/crypto/o_dir.c b/crypto/o_dir.c
--- a/crypto/o_dir.c
+++ b/crypto/o_dir.c
@@ -23,7 +23,10 @@
 #include "internal/o_dir.h"
 
 #define LPDIR_H
-#if defined OPENSSL_SYS_UNIX || defined DJGPP \
+#if defined OPENSSL_NO_POSIX_IO
+/* No file system below the library: directories are not implemented. */
+# include "LPdir_nyi.c"
+#elif defined OPENSSL_SYS_UNIX || defined DJGPP \
     || (defined __VMS_VER && __VMS_VER >= 70000000)
 # include "LPdir_unix.c"
 #elif defined OPENSSL_SYS_VMS
